{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":527},{"id":2,"agency":3,"agency_full":4,"sector":5,"dest":6,"color":7,"year":8,"status":9,"departure_date":10,"arrival_date":11,"transit_days":12,"vehicle":13,"payload":14,"delta_v":15,"data_quality":16,"credit":17,"links":18,"flight_data_quality":37,"fleet_refs":38,"flight":44,"name":495,"type":496,"first":497,"description":498,"events":499,"vehicle_stage":46},"schiaparelli","ESA","European Space Agency + Roscosmos (ExoMars partnership)","gov","MARS","#003247",2016,"FLOWN","2016-03-14","2016-10-19",219,"Proton-M / Briz-M","577 kg (EDM lander part of ExoMars 2016 mission with Trace Gas Orbiter)","~5.5 km/s","good","© European Space Agency. Demonstration EDL lander; impacted at ~540 km/h after parachute jettisoned 3.7 km too early due to IMU saturation. MRO's Context Camera found the impact site the next day; HiRISE imaged it days later.",[19,23,27,30,34],{"l":20,"u":21,"t":22},"Schiaparelli EDM — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schiaparelli_EDM","intro",{"l":24,"u":25,"t":26},"ExoMars 2016 — ESA mission archive","https://www.esa.int/Science_Exploration/Space_Science/ExoMars","core",{"l":28,"u":29,"t":26},"Schiaparelli (NASA NSSDCA)","https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/nmc/spacecraft/display.action?id=2016-017A",{"l":31,"u":32,"t":33},"ESA Schiaparelli landing investigation report (2017)","https://exploration.esa.int/web/mars/-/59176-exomars-2016-schiaparelli-anomaly-inquiry","deep",{"l":35,"u":36,"t":22},"HiRISE imaging of Schiaparelli crash site (UAhirise)","https://www.uahirise.org/ESP_048120_1780","sparse",[39,42],{"id":40,"role":41},"proton-m","launcher",{"id":2,"role":43},"spacecraft",{"launch":45,"cruise":49,"arrival":52,"totals":61,"events":64,"interplanetary_profile":101},{"vehicle_stage":46,"mass_at_tli_kg":47,"source":48},"Proton-M with Briz-M upper stage; ExoMars 2016 launched as TGO+Schiaparelli together",577,"ESA ExoMars 2016 mission archive",{"tcm_count":50,"source":51},3,"ESA mission archive; Schiaparelli separated from TGO 2016-10-16, 3 days before atmospheric entry",{"v_infinity_km_s":53,"periapsis_km":54,"inclination_deg":55,"source":56,"entry_velocity_km_s":57,"edl_system":58,"edl_duration_s":59,"touchdown_velocity_ms":60},5.5,0,7,"ESA mission archive; entry at 121 km altitude, 5.83 km/s",5.83,"parachute_retro",319,130.51,{"total_dv_km_s":53,"tli_or_tmi_dv_km_s":62,"source":63},3.6,"Proton-M/Briz-M Mars transfer capability + ExoMars TCMs + Schiaparelli separation maneuver",[65,69,74,79,83,87,92,96],{"met_days":54,"type":66,"label":67,"description":68},"launch","Launch — Proton-M / Briz-M","Baikonur Cosmodrome, 2016-03-14. ExoMars 2016 carries the Trace Gas Orbiter (TGO) + Schiaparelli EDM (Entry, Descent and Landing Demonstrator Module) — Schiaparelli was a precursor designed to validate ESA's first powered Mars landing technology before the planned 2020 Rosalind Franklin rover.",{"met_days":70,"type":71,"label":72,"description":73},0.01,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-Mars injection","Briz-M upper stage burn sends the stack on a 7-month Mars transfer.",{"met_days":75,"type":76,"label":77,"description":78},30,"tcm","TCM-1","First post-TMI cleanup burn.",{"met_days":80,"type":76,"label":81,"description":82},120,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":84,"type":76,"label":85,"description":86},216,"TCM-3 — final pre-separation","Final approach targeting before Schiaparelli separates from TGO.",{"met_days":88,"type":89,"label":90,"description":91},216.5,"separation","Schiaparelli separation from TGO","2016-10-16. The lander released from the TGO carrier 3 days before atmospheric entry, on a slightly-modified ballistic trajectory toward Meridiani Planum.",{"met_days":12,"type":93,"label":94,"description":95},"edl_or_oi","Schiaparelli EDL — Mars Meridiani Planum","2016-10-19. Parachute deployed at 11 km altitude, retrorockets fired. The lander broke the soft-landing requirement — it transmitted EDL telemetry continuously during descent, ESA's most-important objective.",{"met_days":97,"type":98,"label":99,"description":100},219.01,"anomaly","Lander impact — IMU saturation","The inertial measurement unit saturated during the parachute deceleration, leading the onboard software to believe the lander was already below the surface. It commanded a premature parachute jettison + thrust shutdown at ~3.7 km altitude. Schiaparelli impacted at 540 km/h. Post-mortem identified the software fault; lessons fed into the Rosalind Franklin rover EDL design. TGO entered Mars orbit successfully and continues to operate.",{"source_tier":102,"reference_frame":103,"departure_body":104,"arrival_body":105,"transfer_type":106,"tcm_count":50,"waypoints_helio_au":107},"tier_1_5_hybrid","heliocentric_ecliptic_J2000","earth","mars","type1_lambert",[108,111,115,119,123,127,131,135,139,143,147,151,155,159,162,166,170,174,178,182,186,190,194,198,202,206,210,214,218,222,226,230,234,238,242,246,250,254,258,262,266,270,274,278,282,286,290,294,298,302,306,310,314,317,321,325,329,333,337,341,345,349,353,357,361,365,369,373,377,381,385,389,393,397,401,405,409,413,417,421,425,429,433,437,441,445,449,453,457,461,465,469,473,477,480,483,487,489,491,493],[54,109,54,110],-0.990215,0.139548,[112,113,54,114],2.3228,-0.995196,0.095784,[116,117,54,118],4.6457,-0.998699,0.051863,[120,121,54,122],6.9685,-1.000656,0.007859,[124,125,54,126],9.2913,-1.000883,-0.036158,[128,129,54,130],11.6142,-0.999631,-0.08012,[132,133,54,134],13.937,-0.996782,-0.123956,[136,137,54,138],16.2598,-0.992292,-0.167587,[140,141,54,142],18.5827,-0.986355,-0.210974,[144,145,54,146],20.9055,-0.978809,-0.254017,[148,149,54,150],23.2283,-0.969744,-0.296665,[152,153,54,154],25.5512,-0.959297,-0.338891,[156,157,54,158],27.874,-0.947266,-0.380559,[75,160,54,161],-0.935045,-0.41821,[163,164,54,165],32.5197,-0.919165,-0.462207,[167,168,54,169],34.8425,-0.902956,-0.50198,[171,172,54,173],37.1653,-0.885533,-0.541076,[175,176,54,177],39.4882,-0.866876,-0.57942,[179,180,54,181],41.811,-0.8469,